<!--
Copy to the target repo root as BUGS.md.

Log EVERY non-trivial bug here with reproduction, root cause, and fix, so
patterns become visible across sessions. The value is not the individual row —
it is noticing that four rows across four sessions are the same bug wearing
different clothes.

A bug is "non-trivial" if it took more than a few minutes to understand, or if
the root cause was somewhere other than where the symptom appeared. Typos are
not bugs.

REQUIRED READING FOR THE AGENT: when a test fails, do not proceed to new work
and do not weaken, skip, or delete the test. Reproduce the failure in
isolation, write a minimal failing case if one does not exist, fix the root
cause, then re-run the full suite to confirm nothing else regressed. The row
here gets written after that, not instead of it.

Treat any failure of a foundational-fidelity test as P0: either the change is
wrong, or the spec needs a human decision — which you record and defer rather
than resolve.
-->

